    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="14.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVEg">IV Eg</ref> 14.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="14.2" corresp="#wit-f">⁊ þes eaca sy ús eallum gemæne, þe on þissum íglandum wuniað.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="14.2" corresp="#wit-c">⁊ ðas eaca sy ús eallum gemæne, þe on ðissum iglandum wuniað.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="14.2" corresp="#wit-q">Placet ętiam, ut hoc pactum inconcussum et inuiolabile in reliquum tempus conseruetur,</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="14.2" corresp="#wit-c">⁊ ðæs eaca sy ús eallum gemæne þe on ðissum iglandum wuniað.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-c">But this addition shall apply generally to all of us who dwell in these islands.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Jedoch diese [obige] Ergänzung sei uns allen gemeinsam, die wir auf diesen Inseln wohnen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But let this [above] addition be common to all of us who live in these islands.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares IV Eg 2.2.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
